    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1630">

                <pb facs="1325" n="1209" xml:id="pg1209"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No.819.74/4.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1911-12-21">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 21, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Minister for Foreign Affairs has told me in conversation that his Government
                    will enter into such an understanding as that indicated in your telegram of
                    December 16, if necessary for protecting the canal and the interests of the
                    United States, but hopes such an understanding will not prevent such use of
                    wireless telegraphy as might aid the development of Panama.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dodge.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
